    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d249">

                <pb facs="0516" n="488" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v03/pg488"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">330/8–653: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Mission at the
                        United Nations</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d249-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1953-08-06T19:33:00-04:00">August 6,
                            1953—7:33 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>35. Request you approach Turkish Delegation soonest re Turkish candidacy succeed
                    Greece on SC, following position set forth July 24 letter from Secretary to
                    Lodge.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d249-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d249-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by Paul W. Jones of the Office of UN Political and Security Affairs and
                    concurred in by Paul B. Taylor, Officer in Charge, General Assembly Affairs;
                    cleared with the Bureau of Near Eastern, South Asian and African Affairs; and
                    signed by Assistant Secretary Murphy.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
